## 5. Current Implementation

PSHMP Core v3.1 is a functional implementation rather than a conceptual architecture only.

Approximate scope of the current codebase:

- **Go source code:** on the order of 15,000+ lines  
- **Go source files:** 90+  

Major areas include:

- **pkg/chain/** — dynamic relay chains, PathFinder, Mesh Recovery, verifier  
- **pkg/dht/** — candidate selection, Kademlia-style store, failure tracking  
- **pkg/healing/** — Self-Healing Engine, mesh state machine  
- **pkg/gossip/** — push dissemination and anti-entropy  
- **pkg/delivery/** — DataPath, batch acknowledgements, retransmit cache  
- **pkg/probing/** — K-Factor calculation and adaptive probing  
- **pkg/coordinator/** — optional coordination, sharding, Raft support  
- **pkg/node/** — node lifecycle and management  
- Supporting modules: transport, security, metrics, persistence, config, emulation  

The implementation also includes network emulation tools (demo, stress, extreme, realistic, live modes) and deployment-oriented materials (Docker / Compose).

