## 6. Testing and Demonstrated Results

Testing combines unit tests, network emulation, and limited real-network experiments.

Previously demonstrated internal results include:

| Aspect | Observation |
|--------|-------------|
| Emulated network size | Up to 5,000+ nodes |
| Packet loss scenarios | Up to 25% (and higher in extreme modes) |
| Delivery under tested scenarios | High success rates in emulation (including scenarios reported as 100% under specific test conditions) |
| Recovery behaviour | On the order of hundreds of milliseconds in simulated conditions |
| Control traffic | Substantial reduction with Batch ACK + Gap List (favourable cases approaching ~75%) |

**These results represent internal development and testing conditions.** They must not be interpreted as universal production guarantees. Production performance depends on topology, hardware, traffic, and integration architecture. Physical validation is the responsibility of the acquiring party.

